/-!
# The stage map of a shrinking pair of finite unions of balls

## The target statement (delegated)

`Work.Cohomology.euclidean_stage_split` (file `Submission/Work/Cohomology/euclidean_stage_split.lean`):
for `T = ⋃_{j ∈ Fin k} closedBall (c j) (r j)` and `S = ⋃_{j ∈ Fin l} closedBall (c' j) (r' j)`
finite unions of closed balls in `ℝ^N` (`N ≥ 1`) with `S ⊆ interior T` and with every connected
component of `T` meeting `S` (the hypothesis `hcomp`, phrased with `connectedComponentIn T`), the
map `Work.Cohomology.complMap T S : H_{N-1}(Tᶜ) → H_{N-1}(Sᶜ)` (defined below) admits a left
inverse.

/-- The map on the top homology induced by an inclusion of compact complements

For compact sets `S ⊆ T ⊆ ℝ^N` the complements are ordered `Tᶜ ⊆ Sᶜ`, and the inclusion
`Tᶜ ↪ Sᶜ` induces a map `H_{N-1}(Tᶜ) → H_{N-1}(Sᶜ)`; this is `Work.Cohomology.complMap`.
It is the general form of the "stage map" `Work.Cohomology.stageMap` of
`Submission/Work/Cohomology/CompactComplDefs.lean`.
-/

## Why this is true, and how to prove it

Write `U_T = Tᶜ`, `U_S = Sᶜ` (so `T ⊆ S` and `U_T ⊆ U_S` are open subsets of `ℝ^N`).  The composite
`L_N(T) := H_N(ℝ^N, ℝ^N∖T) → H_{N-1}(Tᶜ) = H_{N-1}(U_T)` of the connecting map of the pair
`(ℝ^N, U_T)` is an isomorphism (`hPairδ_isIso`, using `H_N(ℝ^N) = H_{N-1}(ℝ^N) = 0`), naturally in
`T`; hence the stage map is, up to these isomorphisms, the map
`L_N(T) → L_N(S)` induced by `S ⊆ T` (inclusion of the *excluded* sets).

By Alexander duality (the degree-`0` case) `L_N(T) ≅ ℤ^{c(T)}` is free on the set of connected
components of `T`, and the map `L_N(T) → L_N(S)` is the "componentwise" map: it is injective with
free cokernel exactly when every component of `T` meets `S` (which is `hcomp`).  The splitting is
realized by local degrees: choosing a point `x ∈ K ⊆ S` in each component of `T`, the localization
maps `L_N(T) → L_N({x}) ≅ ℤ` identify `L_N(T)` with `ℤ^{c(T)}`, and the same localizations for `S`
give the inverse on the image.

The available ingredients in this workspace are:

* `Work.Cohomology.Duality.ball_local_homology` — for a nonempty compact convex `D`, `L_N(D) ≅ ℤ`
  is concentrated in degree `N` (the base case);
* `Work.Cohomology.localClass_union_injective` (in progress) — **injectivity** of the localization
  map `L_N(T) → ∏_i L_N({x_i})` for a finite family of compact convex pieces with one point in each;
* `Work.Cohomology.local_generator_convex` — the image of the local fundamental class in `L_N(D)`
  generates, for compact convex `D` (the "surjectivity" half for a single convex piece);
* `Work.Cohomology.exists_inj_fin_compl_union_convex` and
  `Work.Cohomology.free_submodule_of_free_int` — freeness of `L_N(T)` (equivalently of
  `H_{N-1}(Tᶜ)`) for finite unions of compact convex sets, and freeness of submodules of free
  `ℤ`-modules;
* the Mayer–Vietoris long exact sequence of `homologyMV_honest_les` (used in the complement form:
  `covers {U_{T_1}, U_{T_2}}` of `U_{T_1 ∩ T_2}`), which yields, together with the connecting-map
  isomorphisms, the exact sequence
  `L_n(T_1 ∪ T_2) → L_n(T_1) ⊕ L_n(T_2) → L_n(T_1 ∩ T_2) → L_{n-1}(T_1 ∪ T_2)`;
* the vanishing `L_{N-1}(T) = 0` for every finite union `T` of compact convex sets (induction on the
  pieces using this sequence and `ball_local_homology`).

A suggested route: prove the stronger statement for pairs `(T, S)` of finite unions of *compact
convex* sets with `S ⊆ interior T` and every component of `T` meeting `S`, by induction on the
number of pieces of `T`, isolating first the case where `T` is connected (then `L_N(T) ≅ ℤ` is
generated by the local class at any point of `S`), and deducing the general case from the splitting
of `T` into components (`T = C ⊔ (T∖C)`, each part still a finite union of pieces, giving
`L_N(T) ≅ L_N(C) ⊕ L_N(T∖C)`) together with the case analysis on the number of pieces of `S` lying
in each component of `T` (a piece of `T` contained in no piece of `S` contributes a `⊕ℤ` to `T`
and `0` to `S`, hence is split off by the component decomposition).  The finite-generation of all
groups involved lets one conclude "injective with free cokernel" from "injective" plus the explicit
componentwise structure.
-/

namespace Work.Cohomology

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicTopology

/-- The map `H_{N-1}(Tᶜ) → H_{N-1}(Sᶜ)` induced by an inclusion `S ⊆ T` of compact sets
(the complements are then ordered `Tᶜ ⊆ Sᶜ`). -/
def complMap {N : ℕ} (T S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N))) (h : S ⊆ T) :
    ↥((singularChains ℤ (TopCat.of (Set.compl T))).homology (N - 1)) →ₗ[ℤ]
      ↥((singularChains ℤ (TopCat.of (Set.compl S))).homology (N - 1)) :=
  (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap (Work.Cohomology.chainMap ℤ (TopCat.of (Set.compl T))
    (TopCat.of (Set.compl S))
    (inclSet (X := TopCat.of (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N))) (A := Set.compl T)
      (B := Set.compl S) (Set.compl_subset_compl.mpr h))) (N - 1)).hom

end

end Work.Cohomology
